# OUR DASHBOARD — "HAL × Kuwait Financing Cockpit" (spec, not built yet)

**Why we need it (beyond the professor's):** (1) the project says *"Teams will demonstrate a live scenario during the final presentation"* → the dashboard doubles as the **live-scenario engine** (paste Scenario-0 / Scenario-1Y market data → every number updates); (2) the 21-Oct external jury grades content **and presentation quality**; (3) his dashboard has no calculators and is empty for Kuwait rates (see `PROF_DASHBOARD_ANALYSIS.md` §4); (4) one place for the 7-person team to see the same verified numbers (`FACT_BASE.md`).

## 1. Design principles
* **Same brand system as the deck** (`07_Template_Analysis/tokens.json`): HAL red `#CC0000` / deep red `#8B1318`, slate `#2C394D`, greys, Kuwait green `#007A3D` for Kuwait items, navy `#242852` for Track B; light + dark theme; tabular numerals; Arial-compatible stack (`Inter, Arial, sans-serif`). No navy-gold "report" look of the professor's page.
* **One question per view**, action-sentence headers (same as the deck), numbers first, prose second.
* **Every number carries provenance**: hover/click badge → `fact_id`, source file/page, as-of date, status ✅/⚠️/❓ (from FACT_BASE). ❓ values render hatched and cannot feed headline KPIs.
* **Charts = house style** (STYLE_GUIDE §4): no gridlines on bars, labels on bars, forecast shading, bottom legend; Plotly.js with a custom template; "Export PNG @2x" and "Copy as slide-ready image" on every chart.
* **Presentation mode (P key):** full-screen single exhibit, 24 pt+ labels, hides chrome — for the video recording and the live demo.
* **Accessible & responsive:** WCAG AA contrast, keyboard navigation (`1–9` jump to section), works at 360 px.

