## 4. Data model (single compact JSON, ~150 KB, + CSV series)
```
dashboard_data.json
 meta:     {firm:"HAL", country:"Kuwait", ccy:"KWD", asof:"2026-10-02", scenario:"S0", version}
 facts:    [{id:"H10", label, value, unit, source, page, asof, status, definition}]   // from FACT_BASE
 series:   {kwd_usd_daily, kwd_usd_monthly, hal_price, me_asia_quarterly, brent_netlong, ...}  // CSVs in 08_Assets/data
 tables:   {senior_notes (H29), segments_regions (H02-H05b), peers (H33…), esg (B03-B05), conflicts (E1-E14)}
 scenario: {S0:{spot, curve_kwd:[{t,rate}], curve_usd:[{t,rate}]}, S1Y:{…}}                // ◇ pending Scenario Excel
 images:   [{file, caption, source, px}]
```
Rules: no number in HTML text — everything rendered from `facts`/`series`; ranges validated on load (e.g., yields 0–25%, ratios plausible) to prevent the professor's "200% dividend yield" class of bug.

## 5. Calculation specs (must match the project document, FACT_BASE §F)
* Accumulation factor AF(T) = (1 + i_T/2)^{2T} (annual rates, semiannual compounding). FRA a×b: f = 2·[(AF(b)/AF(a))^{1/(2(b−a))} − 1]. Test vectors required in `tests/` (hand-computed examples).
* Bond: face_KWD = 100,000,000 × S₀ (S₀ in KWD per USD; ≈ 0.308 at today's KWD/USD ≈ 3.24 — always use the scenario's S₀); coupon per period = 4%/2 × face; PV = Σ CF_t / (1 + y_t/2)^{2t} (curve-based); YTM = solve Σ CF/(1+y/2)^{k} = price (bisection).
* Forwards: F_t = S₀ × (1+i_quote/2)^{2t} / (1+i_base/2)^{2t} with F in local currency per USD, i_quote domestic, i_base US; hedged USD cost of each KWD payment = payment / F_t(KWD per USD) … state convention on screen.
* IRS: effective rate = bond coupon − floating received + fixed paid (per period), both legs shown; details from the Excel when available.
* Section 8: all-in USD cost = IRR of USD-converted cash flows for each strategy.

## 6. Tech & delivery options
| Option | Pros | Cons |
|---|---|---|
| **A. Claude Artifact (HTML, private link, shareable; can store team state)** — recommended for build/iteration | instant link for the 7 members, no hosting, supports shared state (e.g., portfolio weights, risk scoring) via runtime capabilities | needs the artifact-capabilities/design skills at build time; assets via inline/CDN only |
| B. GitHub Pages single HTML (like the professor) | simple, permanent URL | manual hosting; no shared state without a backend |
| C. Local HTML in the folder | works offline for the live demo | not shareable |
Libraries: Plotly.js (cdnjs), vanilla JS or Alpine; no build step; all data inline. **Offline fallback:** same file saved locally for the live demo.

